{"timestamp":"2026-09-30T08:04:57.846Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"b99d7635-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"one-shot-brief-v1\",\n  \"subject\": \"Financial mathematics\",\n  \"lessonTitle\": \"Compound Interest: Formula, Frequency, and Time\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Contrast simple interest (paid only on the original principal) with compound interest, so viewers see why compounding accelerates growth.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"ce453216-1f31-732b-9dad-404bd4668da0\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Present the compound interest formula A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt) and identify each variable: principal P, annual rate r, compounding periods per year n, and time t.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"3a4e48bb-aae1-7dee-bba3-169cd6d573ac\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Explain how the exponent nt and the term r/n connect compounding frequency and time to the final balance.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"3a4e48bb-aae1-7dee-bba3-169cd6d573ac\", \"d3d7544f-ea65-76da-874a-8c5d37cc0de9\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Show that more frequent compounding (larger n) increases growth, building on the audience's familiarity with rates.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"d3d7544f-ea65-76da-874a-8c5d37cc0de9\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Show that longer time horizons (larger t) increase growth, reinforcing why starting early matters.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"d3d7544f-ea65-76da-874a-8c5d37cc0de9\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notCovered\": [\n    \"Worked numerical examples comparing specific frequencies (e.g., monthly vs. yearly), since the document states effects qualitatively only.\",\n    \"Continuous compounding and the constant e, which the document does not mention.\",\n    \"APY/APR distinctions and real-world account details, which are outside the document's scope.\"\n  ],\n  \"plannedSceneCount\": 6,\n  \"stylePackId\": \"everyday\",\n  \"stylePackReason\": \"Friendly geometric illustration and cobalt/mint palette suit financial literacy for adult learners, keeping the formula and growth ideas approachable.\",\n  \"soundBed\": \"quiet-pulse\",\n  \"soundBedReason\": \"A focused, calm pulse supports a clear intermediate explanation of the formula w","textChunks":["{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"one-shot-brief-v1\",\n  \"subject\": \"Financial mathematics\",\n  \"lessonTitle\": \"Compound Interest: Formula, Frequency, and Time\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Contrast simple interest (paid only on the original principal) with compound interest, so viewers see why compounding accelerates growth.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"ce453216-1f31-732b-9dad-404bd4668da0\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Present the compound interest formula A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt) and identify each variable: principal P, annual rate r, compounding periods per year n, and time t.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"3a4e48bb-aae1-7dee-bba3-169cd6d573ac\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Explain how the exponent nt and the term r/n connect compounding frequency and time to the final balance.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"3a4e48bb-aae1-7dee-bba3-169cd6d573ac\", \"d3d7544f-ea65-76da-874a-8c5d37cc0de9\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Show that more frequent compounding (larger n) increases growth, building on the audience's familiarity with rates.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"d3d7544f-ea65-76da-874a-8c5d37cc0de9\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"point\": \"Show that longer time horizons (larger t) increase growth, reinforcing why starting early matters.\",\n      \"sectionIds\": [\"d3d7544f-ea65-76da-874a-8c5d37cc0de9\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notCovered\": [\n    \"Worked numerical examples comparing specific frequencies (e.g., monthly vs. yearly), since the document states effects qualitatively only.\",\n    \"Continuous compounding and the constant e, which the document does not mention.\",\n    \"APY/APR distinctions and real-world account details, which are outside the document's scope.\"\n  ],\n  \"plannedSceneCount\": 6,\n  \"stylePackId\": \"everyday\",\n  \"stylePackReason\": \"Friendly geometric illustration and cobalt/mint palette suit financial literacy for adult learners, keeping the formula and growth ideas approachable.\",\n  \"soundBed\": \"quiet-pulse\",\n  \"soundBedReason\": \"A focused, calm pulse supports a clear intermediate explanation of the formula w","ithout distracting from the math.\"\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":2036,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":6564,"service":"api","correlationId":"01a0f158-4bfb-76d2-8777-5dc51825cbbc"}}
